     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear TMB users,<br><br>I try to implement a dirichlet distribution as an observation equation in TMB.<br>As far as I see, this distribution is not implemented directly in TMB, but it is in ADMB.<br>I went through ADMB documentation to write this distribution in TMB.<br>My implementation of the log-likelihood works. I could retrieve the parameters of the dirichlet distribution.<br>However, I would like to write a cleaner code, maybe while created the dirichlet log-likelihood function prior to the model with which I can directly write my observations and parameters like:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">nll </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ddirich</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prop_observed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mu_prop</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">true</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><br>Do you have any suggestions ?<br>Thank you.<br><br>Here is my code:<br>I calculate a dirichlet of `N` elements for each time step (t) between 1 and `nt`.<br>The original version is a model in JAGS written as:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  prop_obs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ddirich</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prop</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span></div></code></div><br><br>Based on ADMB doc, the equation of dirichlet is:<br><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-LHyjdTjrQNI/WaPc_k7AbYI/AAAAAAAAAgM/4JRu_XNjRuYOvlevrf30KPDznoFKZkN1QCLcBGAs/s1600/ADMB.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-LHyjdTjrQNI/WaPc_k7AbYI/AAAAAAAAAgM/4JRu_XNjRuYOvlevrf30KPDznoFKZkN1QCLcBGAs/s1600/ADMB.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462559217000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3HPfpcD1bZ-zR7v5HAG17q\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-LHyjdTjrQNI/WaPc_k7AbYI/AAAAAAAAAgM/4JRu_XNjRuYOvlevrf30KPDznoFKZkN1QCLcBGAs/s400/ADMB.png\" width=\"400\" border=\"0\" height=\"48\"></a></p><br>I added some small values (EPS) in log calculations to avoid reaching the range of parameters during optimisation:<br><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-d5toKqwsF-s/WaPddiTnlDI/AAAAAAAAAgQ/Xpy-3AfXvMkkh4F3xwd_HVV7IkoZ8PyLQCLcBGAs/s1600/Negative_LL_TMB.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-d5toKqwsF-s/WaPddiTnlDI/AAAAAAAAAgQ/Xpy-3AfXvMkkh4F3xwd_HVV7IkoZ8PyLQCLcBGAs/s1600/Negative_LL_TMB.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462559217000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0WW_lB-S7TfqEthl0Tdnfe\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-d5toKqwsF-s/WaPddiTnlDI/AAAAAAAAAgQ/Xpy-3AfXvMkkh4F3xwd_HVV7IkoZ8PyLQCLcBGAs/s400/Negative_LL_TMB.png\" width=\"400\" border=\"0\" height=\"34\"></a></p><br>My proposition in TMB is the following:<br>- alpha in the above equation is named `mu_prop` below<br>- `p` in the above equation is named `prop_obs` below. This is the observation.<br><br>The equation has 3 parts:<br>- Gamma sum of each mu that will be `lgamma(mu_prop_bis.sum() + EPS)`<br>- Sum of each Gamma mu named `gammln_each_mu_prop.sum()`<br>- Sum of alpha * log observations that will be ` log_prop_obs_bis.sum()`<br><br>As I calculate also this for each time `t`, the script is a little bit more complicated.<br>Moreover, I sometimes transpose my matrices (then named `bis`) to be able to do sum calculations on columns as it did not work on rows.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">++</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  gammln_each_mu_prop</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lgamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu_prop</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> EPS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  mu_prop_bis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu_prop</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">++</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">++</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    log_prop_obs_bis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu_prop</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prop_obs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> EPS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// Dirichlet negative log-likelihood</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  nll </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lgamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu_prop_bis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">).</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> EPS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gammln_each_mu_F1_m_bis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">).</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log_prop_obs_bis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">).</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">())</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><br><br><br><br></div>"
